ia , cite45†Xinyuan Zhang , cite45†Xinze Zhang , cite129†Xirui Pan , cite130†Xu Zou , cite45†Xunkai Zhang , cite131†Yadi Liu , cite132†Yandong Wu , cite133†Yanfu Li , cite134†Yidong Wang , cite52†Yifan Zhu , cite135†Yijun Tan , cite136†Yilin Zhou , cite137†Yiming Pan , cite138†Ying Zhang , cite139†Yinpei Su , cite140†Yipeng Geng , cite141†Yong Yan , cite135†Yonglin Tan , cite142†Yuean Bi , cite143†Yuhan Shen , cite144†Yuhao Yang , cite133†Yujiang Li , cite131†Yunan Liu , cite134†Yunqing Wang , cite133†Yuntao Li , cite132†Yurong Wu , cite138†Yutao Zhang , cite145†Yuxi Duan , cite138†Yuxuan Zhang , cite59†Zezhen Liu , cite146†Zhengtao Jiang , cite147†Zhenhe Yan , cite148†Zheyu Zhang , cite149†Zhixiang Wei , cite150†Zhuo Chen , cite151†Zhuoer Feng , cite152†Zijun Yao , cite153†Ziwei Chai , cite57†Ziyuan Wang , cite148†Zuzhou Zhang , cite154†Bin Xu , cite155†Minlie Huang , cite23†Hongning Wang , cite89†Juanzi Li , cite156†Yuxiao Dong , cite157†Jie Tang L12: et al. (86 additional authors not shown)  You must enable JavaScript to view entire author list.\nL13: \nL14: View a PDF of the paper titled GLM-5: from Vibe Coding to Agentic Engineering, by GLM-5-Team: Aohan Zeng and 184 other authors\nL15: \nL16: cite158†View PDF cite159†HTML (experimental) L17: > Abstract:We present GLM-5, a next-generation foundation model designed to transition the paradigm of vibe coding to agentic engineering. Building upon the agentic, reasoning, and coding (ARC) capabilities of its predecessor, GLM-5 adopts DSA to significantly reduce training and inference costs while maintaining long-context fidelity.\nL18: To advance model alignment and autonomy, we implement a new asynchronous reinforcement learning infrastructure that drastically improves post-training efficiency by decoupling generation from training. Furthermore, we propose novel asynchronous agent RL algorithms that further improve RL quality, enabling the model to learn from complex, long-horizon interactions more effectively. Through these innovations, GLM-5 achieves state-of-the-art performance on major open benchmarks.\nL19: Most critically, GLM-5 demonstrates unprecedented capability in real-world coding tasks, surpassing previous baselines in handling end-to-end software engineering challenges. Code, models, and more information are available at cite160†this https URL†github.com .\nL20: Subjects:  | Machine Learning (cs.LG); Computation and Language (cs.CL)\nL21: Cite as:  | cite161†arXiv:2602.15763 [cs.LG]\nL22:    | (or cite162†arXiv:2602.15763v2 [cs.LG] for this version)\nL23:    | cite163†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2602.15763†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL24: ## Submission history\nL25: \nL26: From: Aohan Zeng [cite164†view email ]\nL27: cite5†[v1] Tue, 17 Feb 2026 17:50:56 UTC (3,731 KB)\nL28: [v2] Tue, 24 Feb 2026 10:44:44 UTC (3,731 KB)\nL29: \nL30: Full-text links:\nL31: \nL32: ## Access Paper:\nL33: \nL34: View a PDF of the paper titled GLM-5: from Vibe Coding to Agentic Engineering, by GLM-5-Team: Aohan Zeng and 184 other authors\nL35: \nL36:   * cite158†View PDF L37:   * cite159†HTML (experimental) L38:   * cite165†TeX Source L39: \nL40: cite166†view license†creativecommons.org L41: ### Current browse context:\nL42: \nL43: cs.LG\nL44: \nL45: cite167†< prev |   cite168†next > L46: \nL47: cite169†new | cite170†recent | cite171†2026-02 L48: \nL49: Change to browse by:\nL50: \nL51: cite172†cs L52: cite173†cs.CL L53: \nL54: ### References & Citations\nL55: \nL56:   * cite174†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L57:   * cite175†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L58:   * cite176†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L59: \nL60: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL61: \nL62: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL63: \nL64: [Button: ×]\nL65: \nL66: loading...\nL67: \nL6